  "id": "foveal-vision",
  "term": "foveal vision",
  "definition": "Foveal vision is vision by the fovea, the central retinal region that was described here as lacking rods. In this account, looking with the fovea does not show rod-linked effects such as the Purkinje shift, so foveal vision is contrasted with the more peripheral, rod-dependent mode of seeing.",
